          "source_section": "Statement",
          "quote": "Let $x$ be an inertial chart of the affine Minkowski model with coordinates $(x^0,x^1,x^2,x^3)$, let $B:=\\prod_{a=0}^{3}[c_a,d_a]$ with $c_a<d_a$ be a closed axis-parallel box, and let $T$ be a $C^1$ symmetric type-$(2,0)$ tensor field on an open neighbourhood of $B$; put $f^b:=\\partial_aT^{ab}$ (continuous on $B$) as in [[def-sr-stress-energy-tensor-and-force-density]]. (a) (Box identity.) For each $b$, with $F_a^+:=\\{x\\in B:x^a=d_a\\}$, $F_a^-:=\\{x\\in B:x^a=c_a\\}$ and each face integral the Riemann integral over the remaining three coordinates, $$\\int_B f^b\\,d^4x=\\sum_{a=0}^{3}\\Big(\\int_{F_a^+}T^{ab}\\,d^3x-\\int_{F_a^-}T^{ab}\\,d^3x\\Big).$$ (b) (Slice balance.) Write $K:=\\prod_{i=1}^{3}[c_i,d_i]$ and, for $s\\in[c_0,d_0]$, $Q^b(s):=\\int_K T^{0b}(s,x)\\,d^3x$; this is finite and continuous in $s$. For $c_0\\le s_1<s_2\\le d_0$, $$Q^b(s_2)-Q^b(s_1)=\\int_{[s_1,s_2]\\times K} f^b\\,d^4x-\\sum_{i=1}^{3}\\Big(\\int_{[s_1,s_2]\\times K_i^+}T^{ib}\\,d^3x-\\int_{[s_1,s_2]\\times K_i^-}T^{ib}\\,d^3x\\Big),$$ where $K_i^\\pm$ are the two faces $x^i=d_i$, $x^i=c_i$ of $K$. (c) (Finite-flux conservation.) If $f=0$ on $[s_1,s_2]\\times K$ and $T^{ib}=0$ on the side faces $[s_1,s_2]\\times K_i^\\pm$ for $i=1,2,3$, then $Q^b(s_1)=Q^b(s_2)$ for every $b$. The theorem concerns finite axis-parallel boxes in one inertial chart and is proved by the fundamental theorem of calculus. It does not assert a flux identity for arbitrary regions or hypersurfaces, does not assert that $Q^b$ transforms as a four-vector under a change of inertial chart, and asserts no conservation without the stated side-flux hypothesis; no noncompact or limiting statement is made. No choice principle is used.",
